  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When n-Hexane is heated with anhydrous&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AlCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>&nbsp;gas at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>573</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;under a pressure of about&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>35</mn><mi>atm</mi></math>&nbsp;it Isomerises to give a branched chain alkanes.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><munder><mi>HCl</mi><mo>&#9651;</mo></munder><mrow><mi>Anhy</mi><mo>.</mo><msub><mi>AlCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></munderover><munder><mrow><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CHCH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>methylpentane</mi></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>methylpentane</mi></math></p><p>Major product in the above reaction is 2-methylpentane.</p>"
